From: Custom V4L2 HW Encode Patches
Subject: Enable V4L2 hardware encoding for Hantro H1 encoder on i.MX8MM

This patch enables hardware video encoding via the V4L2 Hantro H1 encoder
on NXP i.MX8MM platforms. Ported from Chromium 117 to 129.0.6668.100.

Changes:
1. Remove VP9 software encoder from WebRTC to force H264/VP8 HW codec selection
2. Fix chrome://gpu display status for video encode on Linux (V4L2, not just VAAPI)
3. Use MMAP for ALL encoder input (both shmem and GpuMemoryBuffer) to avoid
   DMABUF data_offset bug on non-ChromeOS Linux
4. Add MMAP buffer handling for both SHMEM and GpuMemoryBuffer frames
5. Add MMAP case to plane size setup loop (fixes "contiguous mapping too small")
6. Disable low-resolution software fallback to keep HW encoder active
7. Fix NV12 GPU memory buffer usage flag for zero-copy capture path
   (use VEA_READ_CAMERA_AND_CPU_READ_WRITE instead of GPU_READ_CPU_READ_WRITE)
   Note: IsGpuMemoryBufferNV12Supported force-true is in separate patch
8. Stride-aware row-by-row copy with dst_stride derived from MMAP buffer size
   (fixes green bars when source stride != encoder stride, fixes low-res VP8)
9. Prefer HW encoder formats over SW formats in codec negotiation

Tested on: NXP i.MX8MM EVK with Chromium 129.0.6668.100

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [i.MX specific]

